# is the worked example; the load-bearing scholarly contribution is the
# companion paper (in submission). Cite the paper when it is in print;
# this file is the citable handle for the artefact itself.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use art-project in research, teaching, or practice, please cite this software entry. The companion paper is in submission to *Digital Creativity* (Routledge / Taylor & Francis); once published, prefer the paper citation."
title: "art-project: a pre-studio articulation scaffold for practice-based artistic research (Claude Code plugin)"
abstract: "A Claude Code plugin offering six modes (socratic / provoke / lineage / brief / rehearsal / ideate) for the propositional articulation phase that precedes studio work in practice-based artistic research. Encodes a cognitive-scaffold position (Clark & Chalmers 1998; Malafouris 2013; Penny 2017), a tradition-tag reference layer with Authentic Practice Boundaries, and a measured-harm disclosure. Bilingual English / Korean wiki at apesuite.org/plugins/."
